# Fixed-token rows of litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B on the Galaxy S26 in the weekly job (schedule.json
# devices.s26.extra_cells, tag stress, since 2026-11-04, D-557): context 2048, decode 256
# (Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm, Hub main LFS sha256 25447e25..., 964,566,992 B):
#   - the protocol row, native-benchmark-1024x256 (methodology/agreed-protocol-gemma4.md "The spec"), LiteRT-LM GPU on the
#     side build v0.19.0-pregpu and CPU on the flat pinned build: the two payload rows of
#     matrices/d541-qwen35-s26-android.cells byte for byte (the file the team page defines this phone's Qwen3.5-0.8B
#     protocol cells from), so each weekly session measures those cells again (the CPU row's six records of 2026-11-04 all
#     fell past the 15 % line of cpu-cap-rule, 43.7-53.0 %, and pool into no number);
#   - three prefill stress counts around the file's prefill signatures (prefill_1024, prefill_512, ... prefill_1):
#     17 = 16 + 1, 1023 = 1024 - 1, 1025 = 1024 + 1, LiteRT-LM GPU on the same side build: the rows of
#     matrices/d557-qwen35-s26-stress-gpu-android.cells byte for byte (first run by hand 2026-11-04,
#     results/raw/2026-11-04-d557-qwen35-stress-gpu-s26-android).
# The session anchor first, as in every Android half and extra file (the job re-judges each payload session by its own
# anchor records). No runs= (the runner's default of 3 runs per row, round by round), no cooldown= (the runner's 120 s,
# the 0.6B / 1.7B class: docs/dashboard-cells-v1.md).
# Needs the side build on the phone, /data/local/tmp/llmbench/engines/v0.19.0-pregpu (android/README.md, "Side builds";
# kept there since D-449): without it the job skips this session and runs the rest of the sitting.
# Estimate: about 1 h = the anchor row 5 min + three rounds of four GPU launches (120 s cooldown + up to 112 s of GPU
# engine creation + about 15 s each) and one CPU launch (120 + about 25 s), plus any gate re-run (a GPU row's block of
# three: about 12 min).
# The week: with every device attached all 14 firings are taken (docs/dashboard-recurring-job-v1.md section 11), and after the
# NPU session this file does not fit before release_by: it stays left that week and runs at the first firing a device leaves
# free (schedule.json, this entry's _doc).
#   BENCH_CPU_MASK= ./bench matrix matrices/dashboard-stress-v1-s26-android.cells --platform android
android llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF short-chat anchor=1 runs=3 file=Qwen3-0.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=gpu engine-build=v0.19.0-pregpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=cpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-17x256 backend=gpu engine-build=v0.19.0-pregpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-1023x256 backend=gpu engine-build=v0.19.0-pregpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-1025x256 backend=gpu engine-build=v0.19.0-pregpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048
